hi  my name is ryan and this is an  introduction to assured workloads  in the next few minutes we'll talk about  how you can make sure that the right  controls are in place so you can run  regulated workloads on google cloud  ready let's get started  [Music]  regulatory compliance can be a challenge  for governments and businesses looking  to use the cloud  some workloads or types of data may have  strict compliance requirements  surrounding data residency data access  and personnel access  at the same time you still want to be  able to use the latest most innovative  cloud services  this is where assured workloads comes  into play  assured workloads is a tool that helps  you run secure and compliant workloads  on google cloud  all organizations have to do is choose  the right regulatory framework and  google cloud will put the necessary  cloud controls in place to support your  compliance requirements across the globe  assured workload supports compliance  with platform controls to create  regulated boundaries on public cloud  infrastructure there are several  platform controls you can choose from  including favorite moderate fedramp high  criminal justice information systems u.s  regions and support  impact level 4 hipaa high trust  eu regions and support and eu regions in  support with sovereignty controls  two areas where these platform controls  help organizations meet compliance  requirements our data residency and  personnel data access controls  first there's data residency for at rest  and in use  assured workloads restricts the regions  you can select for your resources based  on which platform control you choose for  example if you select us regions and  support your resources will be  restricted to u.s regions  if a developer at your organization  tries to create a resource that will  store data at rest in a different region  the action will be blocked and logged  second there's personnel data access  controls  these ensure that only google personnel  who are able to satisfy certain physical  location and background check  requirements are able to access customer  data in the course of a support action  for example if you select fedramp high  support access will be limited to google  personnel who are located in the u.s and  have completed enhanced background  checks  beyond data residency and personnel data  access controls assured workloads  provides customers with security best  practices for key management based on  the compliance requirements of the  organization  a key provision of many regulations is  that organizations need to manage their  own encryption keys  for compliance regimes like il4 assured  workloads mandates customer managed  encryption keys  a key management project is created and  is separated from resource folders to  establish separation of duties between  security administrators and developers  assured workloads also creates a key  ring to store your keys  strong encryption key management and  separation of duties all support  positive security and compliance  outcomes on google cloud for other  compliance regimes customers are able to  receive google manage encryption keys  which by default are fips 142 compliant  assured workloads also supports cloud  kms customer managed encryption keys  cloud external key manager and key  import  assured workloads can also help with  data sovereignty using assured workloads  for eu regions and support with  sovereignty controls  this means that customers in europe have  mechanisms to exercise independent  control over the cloud provider's access  to their data approving access only for  specific provider behaviors deemed  appropriate and necessary by the  customer providing protections against  legal seizure  getting started is easy you can create a  new assured workloads folder by visiting  the google cloud console selecting a  google cloud organization and going to  the compliance section  you will fill out a brief onboarding  stepper selecting options for geographic  jurisdiction compliance type region  folder configuration and key management  fedrate moderate is offered at no  additional cost to customers so you can  begin using it today  in future videos we'll take a closer  look at how to get started  let's take a look at an example use case  a large technology provider to the us  government needed to respond to a  large-scale geopolitical incident which  created new requirements for compliance  the customer was able to expand their  regulatory boundary on google cloud to  meet new compliance and data residency  requirements while still restricting  personnel access controls to us persons  and maintaining their nist 853  and nist 800 171 security controls on  google cloud  after the incident was resolved the  customer was able to rapidly resort to  their regulatory boundary  assured workloads makes adapting to new  compliance requirements easy allowing  the customer to quickly set up or expand  a regulated boundary to maintain  compliance while still being able to use  google cloud's latest innovative  technologies in any of our regions  sometimes an organization will need more  than just one compliance regime for  their cloud resources  let's take a look at an example of a  multinational business that operates in  europe the united states and canada  a top-level folder is created and  registered under which all regulated  workloads live  within the top level folder are  subfolders created by the assured  workloads api for different compliance  regimes that the business needs  in this case there are compliance  regimes for eu regions and support  dod impact level 4 and can regions and  support  within each sub-boulder are the projects  that are subjected to each compliance  regime  all cloud resources within these folders  follow the specific controls and guard  rails to support compliance  so there you have it an overview of what  assured workloads is and how it can help  you more easily run secure and compliant  workloads on google cloud  if you want to learn more visit  cloud.google.com  slash assured workloads  and stay tuned for more episodes of  assured workloads 101 where we'll walk  through how to use assured workloads us  and eu compliance and how to build with  compliance in mind  thanks for watching  [Music]  you

